    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for perineurioma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Section contributors - separate source citation not necessary",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 16.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none; \" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: transparent; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Intraneural perineurioma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\"><em style=\"\">Essential:</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pseudo&ndash;onion bulb pattern on cross-section, with axons in the centre</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">AND</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Tumour cells are positive for at least one perineurial antigen (EMA, claudin-1, GLUT1) and negative for S100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: transparent; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">Soft tissue perineurioma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\"><em style=\"\">Essential:</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Slender spindle cells with bipolar cytoplasmic processes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">AND</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Storiform and/or whorled architecture</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>AND</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"605\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Tumour cells are positive for at least one perineurial antigen (EMA, claudin-1, GLUT1) and negative for S100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
